                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "673f2682-f2a5-4f4f-b79e-5ad94b9356e5",
                        "source_entry_id": "5cc1098d-1c57-31fe-a8a0-4655338f7858",
                        "source_sense_id": "633f0f0d-87ed-3d77-924b-2e4d06369c1c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Medizin: eine vollständige Lähmung der Skelettmuskeln",
                        "target_lang_word": "palsy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "palsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f8ac838-22d2-3d01-bf9b-f650be96cd83",
                                        "entry_id": "e5274b45-c2ec-3898-85bb-624e6e78973f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mate, chum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ea0cfa2-a105-45f8-abc9-c2d42b4d2154",
                                                "sense_id": "4f8ac838-22d2-3d01-bf9b-f650be96cd83",
                                                "text": "Listen, palsy, you're not the boss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "palsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e67af9d3-9ce6-359d-b00d-a3c4cfb84ae7",
                                        "entry_id": "32544ffa-e6f0-3973-8401-637951a51ba9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Complete or partial muscle paralysis of a body part, often accompanied by a loss of feeling and uncontrolled body movements such as shaking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42f25a0e-96e5-4a63-b3d8-2ed4f8bdd1d2",
                                                "sense_id": "e67af9d3-9ce6-359d-b00d-a3c4cfb84ae7",
                                                "text": "The palsie plagues my pulses\nwhen I prigg yoͬ: piggs or pullen\nyour culuers take, or matchles make\nyour Chanticleare or sullen"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84372908-2ad8-47eb-9059-127a8e7ac1d5",
                                                "sense_id": "e67af9d3-9ce6-359d-b00d-a3c4cfb84ae7",
                                                "text": "\"Young lady, there is no hope; one side of the Duchesse is struck with palsy; she retains her senses, and will, most probably, to the last; but she cannot live through the night.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4620630-7fba-4f9d-895e-c8ffd47ca93e",
                                                "sense_id": "e67af9d3-9ce6-359d-b00d-a3c4cfb84ae7",
                                                "text": "\"Ah! now we come to business! Barber, who's dead?\"\n \"Alderman Croten, sir.\"\n\"Tut-tut. Croten gone?\"\n\"Yes, sir; palsy took him at a ripe age. And Abel's gone, the Town Crier;\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58b18708-c5a1-4373-ac29-d1eed4a9cd01",
                                                "sense_id": "e67af9d3-9ce6-359d-b00d-a3c4cfb84ae7",
                                                "text": "Again we were stricken of our palsy, slowed down, re-accelerated, and there, at last, were the few huts of a hamlet, with the lorry, lying at an angle in the road's camber, outside a tea-shop."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "palsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0771923-09a2-3c08-a599-d815d9106e70",
                                        "entry_id": "84a221bc-5151-31f8-b136-def607caaa7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To paralyse, either completely or partially."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4e17940-6644-4fae-9829-1389387779ec",
                                                "sense_id": "a0771923-09a2-3c08-a599-d815d9106e70",
                                                "text": "1831, William Lloyd Garrison, The Liberator, To The Public http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/aia/part4/4h2928t.html\nIn the month of August, I issued proposals for publishing \"THE LIBERATOR\" in Washington city; but the enterprise, though hailed in different sections of the country, was palsied by public indifference."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6925749b-52c5-4977-91a7-e72222ada660",
                                                "sense_id": "a0771923-09a2-3c08-a599-d815d9106e70",
                                                "text": "Its streets were blocked up with snow - the few passengers seemed palsied with snow, and frozen by the ungenial visitation of winter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "palsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8defd18f-093d-3314-b242-4a18acb207e5",
                                        "entry_id": "453cc399-42fe-3d17-9a09-569b57da8a0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chummy, friendly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4dc28062-0719-42f7-94d8-a16d91bab7c4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5cc1098d-1c57-31fe-a8a0-4655338f7858",
                        "source_sense_id": "633f0f0d-87ed-3d77-924b-2e4d06369c1c",
